# API of the {{ twin_name }} twin

Root: `${{ '{' }}{{ base_url_env }}}/api/v1`. Every request needs `Authorization: Bearer ${{ '{' }}{{ token_env }}}`, except `GET /healthz` (outside the root), which only says the service is up.

The authoritative description, with every parameter and response schema, is `GET /api/v1/openapi.json`. This file is the short form.

## Parameters many endpoints share

| Parameter | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `at` | version to read: `head` (default), a commit id, `#<n>`, or an ISO 8601 time with an offset |
| `branch` | branch to read; default `main` |
| `format` | `json` (default), `arrow`, `parquet`; or an `Accept` header of `application/vnd.apache.arrow.stream` or `application/vnd.apache.parquet` |
| `limit` | most rows of any table (listings, `/graph/edges`, `/block/*`, versions, logs); JSON default 100 and at most 10,000; Arrow and Parquet return everything unless given |
| `cursor` | `next_cursor` of the previous page |
| `columns`, `properties`, `types`, `edge_types`, `uids` | lists: repeat the parameter or separate values with commas |

Responses that read data name the version they read: `"version": {"id", "seq", "t"}` in JSON; `x-dta-version-id`, `x-dta-version-seq`, `x-dta-version-t` headers on Arrow and Parquet.

## Meta

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /meta/health` | twin id and name, tier, head version, number of versions, fidelity state, manifest revision and hash; `clock` (`kind`, `available`, `now`: the twin's time); `sync` (`interval`, `staleness`, `freshness_s`, `fresh`, `questions`, `sources`, `last_run`, `job`), null for a static twin; `compute` (`worker`: whether the twin has one and whether it answers; `questions`: how many are validated, provisional and failing; `job`: the compute job in progress) |
| `GET /meta/schema?at=` | object and link types with ancestors, link ends and properties (kind, unit, required, role, description); abstract classes with their concrete kinds; enums |
| `GET /meta/schema/linkml?at=` | the same schema as LinkML text |
| `GET /meta/manifest?at=` | the twin's manifest: contract, sources (without secrets), mappings |

## Objects

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /objects/{type}?columns=&where=&sort=&count=&include=provenance` | objects of a type (or of an abstract class), paged in uid order, or in the order of `sort` (`<property>`, or `-<property>` for descending; objects without a value last) |
| `GET /objects?uid_like=&types=&include_meta=&count=` | `uid` and `type` of every object, of any type, whose uid matches an SQL pattern (`%` any run of characters, `_` one), in uid order; the twin's own record types are left out unless `types` names them or `include_meta=true` |
| `GET /objects/{type}/{uid}?include=provenance` | one object |
| `GET /object/{uid}` | one object, whatever its type |
| `GET /search?q=&types=&include_meta=&count=` | `uid`, `type` and `name` of every object, of any type, whose uid or whose name matches an SQL pattern, in uid order; one request instead of one per type |
| `GET /objects/{type}/{uid}/links?direction=out\|in\|both&edge_types=&edge_where=` | the object's edges and what is at their other end |
| `GET /objects/{type}/{uid}/history?range=&properties=` | one row per version in which the object changed |

`where` is repeated: `<property>:<op>:<value>` with `eq ne lt le gt ge in like null notnull`.

`count=true` adds the number of rows of the whole listing, all pages: `total` in JSON, the header `x-dta-total` in every format.

## Graph

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /graph/neighbors?seed=&depth=&direction=&edge_types=&edge_where=&limit=` | nodes within `depth` hops of the seeds, with type and depth, and the edges between them |
| `GET /graph/paths?source=&target=&max_depth=&k=&weight=&direction=&edge_types=&edge_where=` | up to `k` simple paths of at most `max_depth` hops (default 6, at most 64), shortest first; each path has `nodes`, `edges` (each with `src`, `dst`, `edge_type`, `link_uid`), `hops` and `cost` |
| `POST /graph/subgraph` body `{seeds, depth, direction, edge_types, edge_where, node_types, limit, properties}`; `part=nodes\|edges` picks the table for Arrow and Parquet | the part of the graph reached from the seeds |
| `GET /graph/edges?edge_types=&edge_where=` | every edge: `src`, `dst`, `edge_type`, `link_uid` |

`edge_where` is repeated: `<LinkType>.<property>:<op>:<value>`, with the operators of `where`. A link of that type is followed, and returned, only when it passes; the name may be an abstract class, which stands for every link type under it. Links of types the filter does not name, and references, are not affected: combine it with `edge_types` to follow nothing else.

## History

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /history/versions?from=&to=&cause=&actor=&run=&backfill=&order=asc\|desc` | versions with their time, cause, actor and note |
| `GET /history/versions/{selector}` | the one version a selector names |
| `GET /history/diff?from=&to=&types=&detail=summary\|rows` | rows added, modified and removed per type, or the rows themselves |
| `GET /history/branches` | branches and their heads |

## Block (whole tables)

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /block/nodes/{type}?columns=` | every object of a type at a version |
| `GET /block/edges/{edge_type}` | every edge of one type, with the link's properties |
| `GET /block/slice/{type}?range=&properties=&uids=&mode=state\|changes&layout=long\|tensor` | the type's objects over a range of versions |
| `POST /block/training-set` body `{target, uids, start, end, branch, step, features, ahead, horizon}` | a frame for learning: one row per object and grid time (`unique_id`, `ds`, `y`, a column per feature and, with `horizon`, `label` and `label_ds`), every value the one stored at or before its time; `meta` (schema metadata `dta:training` in Arrow and Parquet) says what the rows hold |

As JSON these are paged like every other table; as Arrow or Parquet they come whole.

## Sync

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /sync/sources` | per source: `status` (`ok`, `failing`, `disabled`), `last_error`, `watermark` (the time of its newest data), `last_success_at`, `freshness_s`, its `datasets` with how far each has been read, its `mappings`; and the twin's `clock` |
| `GET /sync/runs?status=&kind=` | the runs that loaded or synced the twin, newest first: `status` (`running`, `succeeded`, `partial`, `failed`), `kind` (`backfill`, `incremental`, `replay`), when it started and finished, versions and rows written, rows set aside and late, `error` |
| `GET /sync/runs/{uid}` | one run |
| `GET /sync/runs/{uid}/rejects?rule=&mapping=` | the rows the run set aside (which row, which rule it broke and why; never the row's values); `total` counts the rows that pass the filters; a cursor is refused once the file has changed: start again |
{% if live %}
| `POST /sync/runs`, body `{}`, `{"sources": [...]}` or `{"replay": {"source": ..., "dataset": ...}}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | starts a run now and answers `{"job": {...}}`: 202 for a new job, 200 when the same run is already queued or running |
{% endif %}

## Lifecycle

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /lifecycle/jobs?kind=&state=&lane=` | work the API does in the background, newest first: `id`, `kind`, `lane` (`sync` for sync runs, `compute` for other long work; the jobs of a lane run one at a time, in order), `state` (`queued`, `running`, `succeeded`, `failed`), `result`, `error`, `trace_id`, `duration_ms` |
| `GET /lifecycle/jobs/{id}` | one job, as `{"data": {...}}` |
| `GET /lifecycle/logs?level=&since=&context=&trace_id=&service=&limit=` | the twin's own structured log lines, newest first |
| `POST /lifecycle/register` body `{"code": <sha256>\|null}` | brings the twin's functions, models and questions in line with its manifest in one version, and none when nothing differs: `functions`, `models` and `questions`, each with what was `created`, `changed` and left `unchanged`, and the `version`. `code` is the hash `POST /artifacts` gave for the twin's packed code |

## Functions

What the twin computes: shipped built-ins with the arguments their registration fixes, and code the twin brought, which runs in the twin's worker.

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /functions` | every function: `id`, `kind` (`builtin`, `registered`), `entry`, the fixed `params`, `latency_budget_ms`, `origin` (`manifest`, `runtime`), `status` (`active`, `disabled`) |
| `GET /functions/{id}` | one function, with `parameters`: what its entry takes and which of them are fixed |
| `POST /functions/{id}/run?at=&branch=` body: the arguments by name (a built-in's may be given in the query string instead) | the answer: `value` (a JSON value, or the rows of a table, paged; Arrow and Parquet as elsewhere), `unit`, `interval`, `notes`, the `version` read, `function`, `model`, `provisional` and `reasons`. The function is the one registered now; `at` chooses the data it reads. A function that gives rows to write names the version it wrote in `wrote`; any other run writes nothing |
| `POST /functions` body `{id, entry, params, description, latency_budget, env, artifact}` | registers a function while the twin runs: 201 with the function |
| `DELETE /functions/{id}` | disables a function registered while the twin ran |

## Questions

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /questions?status=` | every question with what it may claim: `status` (`validated`, `provisional`, `failing`), `reason`, `metric`, `measured_error`, `tolerance`, `unit`, `basis` (`backtest`, `noise_floor`, `latency`), its `function` and active `model` |
| `GET /questions/{id}` | one question |
| `POST /questions/{id}/answer?at=&branch=` body: arguments of its function | the answer of the question's function, as `POST /functions/{id}/run` gives it; `provisional` with `reasons` while the question is not validated, the note `question_failing` when it was measured outside its tolerance |
| `POST /questions/measure` body `{"questions": [...]}` or `{}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | starts a job that measures the questions against their tolerances and records what each may claim; answers `{"job": {...}}`, 202 for a new job, 200 when it exists |

## Models

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /models?spec=&status=&question=` | every candidate of every model specification: `uid` (`twin_model:<spec>/<candidate>`), `family`, `params`, `target`, `features`, `status` (`candidate`, `active`, `rejected`, `retired`), what it was fitted on |
| `GET /models/{uid}` | one model, with `state`: the header of its fitted state (range and series fitted, validity, library versions) |
| `GET /models/{uid}/backtests` | its evaluations, newest first: range, origins, horizon, error and the baseline's, every score, whether it was accepted |
| `POST /models/evaluate` body `{"spec": ..., "budget_s": ...}` or `{}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | starts a job that backtests every candidate, makes the best accepted one `active` with a fitted state and records the question's status, in one version; answers `{"job": {...}}`, 202 or 200 |
| `POST /models/{uid}/predict?at=&branch=` body `{horizon, levels, interventions}` | `unique_id`, `ds`, `mean` and `lo_<level>`, `hi_<level>` per level, for `horizon` steps after the version; `notes` (`outside_validity`, `no_intervals`) |
| `POST /models` body `{spec, candidate, family \| artifact + entry, params, target, features, question, interventional}` | registers a candidate while the twin runs: 201 with the model |
| `DELETE /models/{uid}` | retires a model registered while the twin ran |

## Scenarios

What the twin would be under assumed changes, each on a branch of its own.

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `GET /scenarios?include_deleted=` | every scenario: `id`, `name`, `branch`, `base_version`, `base_t`, `interventions`, `horizon`, `step`, `models`, `status` (`created`, `running`, `done`, `failed`, `deleted`) |
| `GET /scenarios/{id}` | one scenario, with whether its branch `exists` and where the branch's `head` is |
| `POST /scenarios?at=` body `{name, description, interventions: [{target, uid, value, start, end}], horizon, models}` | makes a scenario from a version of `main`: 201, or 200 with `created: false` when the same request at the same base was made before |
| `POST /scenarios/{id}/run` body `{"budget_s": ...}` or `{}`, optional header `Idempotency-Key` | starts a job in which each model predicts the horizon and the branch gains one version per grid time; answers `{"job": {...}}`, 202 or 200 |
| `GET /scenarios/{id}/compare?targets=&against=&uids=` | `target`, `uid`, `t`, `scenario`, `against`, `difference` on the scenario's grid; `against` is `main` or another scenario of the same base |
| `DELETE /scenarios/{id}` | removes the scenario's branch and marks its record `deleted` |

A scenario's branch is read like any other: pass `branch=<its branch>` to the endpoints above.

## Derived data

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `POST /derived` body `{branch, type, rows, kind, source, inputs_version, confidence, t_valid}` | writes rows that were worked out (`kind`: `inferred`, `assumed`, `simulated`) as one version, each value carrying its `source` (the uid of a function or model) and the version of its inputs: 201 with `{"version", "rows"}`. Observed facts, assumed or simulated facts on `main`, and properties a source fills are refused. At most 100,000 rows and 16 MiB |

## Artifacts

Files kept outside the graph, named by the SHA-256 of their content: code, fitted models, large tables.

| Endpoint | Returns |
|---|---|
| `POST /artifacts` | keeps the request body (any bytes, at most 512 MiB) and answers `{"sha256", "size_bytes", "location"}`: 201 when new, 200 when the same content was already kept. Nothing is written to the graph |
| `GET /artifacts/{sha256}` | the file's bytes; 404 `artifact.not_found` when none is kept under that hash |

## What changes the twin

Each of these writes a new version on `main`, or on a scenario's branch:

- registrations: `POST /lifecycle/register` (no version when nothing differs), `POST /functions`, `DELETE /functions/{id}`, `POST /models`, `DELETE /models/{uid}`;
- evaluations and measurements: `POST /models/evaluate` records the backtests, the active model and its question's status; `POST /questions/measure` records what each question may claim;
- scenarios: `POST /scenarios` and `DELETE /scenarios/{id}` record the scenario on `main`; `POST /scenarios/{id}/run` writes the predictions on the scenario's branch and the run's status on `main`;
- derived data: `POST /derived`;
- running a function that gives rows to write, through `POST /functions/{id}/run` or by answering a question it answers: the answer names the version written in `wrote`;
{% if live %}
- sync runs: `POST /sync/runs` makes the twin read its sources, which is the only way new observed data arrives.
{% endif %}

These never change it: every `GET`; answering a question and running a function, when the function gives no rows to write; predicting (`POST /models/{uid}/predict`); `POST /graph/subgraph`; `POST /block/training-set`. `POST /artifacts` keeps a file and writes nothing to the graph.

There is no endpoint that edits observed data: {% if live %}it changes only when the sources do and a sync run reads them{% else %}a static twin's data was loaded once and does not change{% endif %}.

Jobs are kept in the API's memory and are forgotten when it restarts. The lasting record of a sync run is in `/sync/runs`, of an evaluation in `/models/{uid}/backtests` and `/questions`, of a scenario in `/scenarios`.
